+## Local process identity
+
+Orca task metadata has a private `state/<id>.orca-process` launch binding owned by `bin/fm-orca-process-lib.sh`.
+The binding ties one task generation to the terminal handle, PTY, incarnation, tab, leaf, local execution host, worktree identity, and surviving interactive shell PID, birth time, tty, and working directory.
+A passive read revalidates those facts against Orca and the local kernel before examining the terminal foreground process group.
+A recognized foreground harness is `alive`; the exact bound shell as the sole foreground process is `dead`.
+A foreign foreground process is `ambiguous`, a legacy record without a binding is `unverified`, and a mismatched or unreadable identity is `unreadable`.
